cy's \"cancer\" has no qualifier, so it matches the DiseaseClass pattern.\n  - **Linguistic Rule (Proposed):** Determine entity type from the lexical specificity of the disease span before considering its syntactic context.\n    1. If the span is a bare generic category label (e.g., cancer, disease, syndrome, tumor, mental retardation) with no organ, etiologic, eponymous, or acronym qualifier, label it **DiseaseClass**, even inside \"family history of,\" \"associated with,\" or \"characterized by\" frames.\n    2. Assign **Modifier** only when the span is a specific, qualified disease name (site, eponym, or acronym) functioning as an attributive or history/context qualifier of another noun.\n    3. Flag bare prenominal category terms (\"cancer cases\") for manual verification, because the provided data does not resolve them.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 3816, "output_tokens": 7394, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 6292}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}